      "sequence_position": 2,
      "problem": "Given the sets $X={♠,◻,♡,♢,△}$ and $Y={♠,◻,♣,♡},$ find $X∖Y.$",
      "worked_solution": "The set  $X∖Y$ is the set of all elements belonging to $X$ but *not* $Y.$ Note that the elements $♠,◻,♡\\in X$ are also in $Y,$ so we must remove them. Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X∖Y & =X-Y \\\\  & ={♠,◻,♡,♢,△}-{♠,◻,♣,♡} \\\\  & ={△,♢}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
